630	The statements of this section are not named results of the source article.  They isolate, as exact identities, the register bookkeeping that relates the six-register presentation used in Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} to the two local extraction blocks $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and $\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, and to the register order in which the auxiliary state is already known to be normalized.  Nothing here constructs an extraction isometry, and nothing here proves an approximation estimate: every identity below holds for arbitrary operators and arbitrary vectors, and the only hypotheses that appear are explicit isometry or unitarity equations for the operators involved.
